{
  "title": "Third declension: family and people",
  "note": "Third-declension nouns have genitive -is, and the nominative often hides the stem, so learn both forms: rex, regis (m), stem reg-. Singular: (varies), -is, -i, -em, -e. Plural: -es, -um, -ibus, -es, -ibus. Gender is learned word by word, but words for men are masculine and words for women feminine.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Allen and Greenough, 3rd Declension",
    "u": "https://dcc.dickinson.edu/grammar/latin/3rd-declension-classes"
  },
